  "reason": "Existing RNA-only evidence shows that multiprofile modeling strongly improves performance, with scVI_n200 plus avgpool/transformer reaching about 0.65 accuracy, while PCA_n2000 multiprofile avgpool reaches 0.591. The missing PCA_n2000 multiprofile transformer result leaves uncertainty about whether transformer aggregation helps a simpler RNA representation and whether the scVI advantage is robust across aggregation choices. config_003 tests this directly while keeping the model RNA-only and the profile setting multiprofile, making it a clean comparison to config_002 and the scVI multiprofile results. It is the best next experiment because it completes an important RNA-only design comparison, has high expected performance, and avoids confounding the next step with image or fusion choices."
}

